---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { pages, site } from '../site';

const meta = pages['/about/'];
const article = 'https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/lazy-optimizer-why-we-need-stop-calling-ai-henard-gertzen-dnpef/';
---

<Base title={meta.title} description={meta.description} image="/og/about.png">
  <header class="page-head narrow">
    <p class="kicker">About</p>
    <h1>Hi, I’m Henard</h1>
  </header>

  <div class="narrow about-body">
    <p class="lede">
      I’m a software developer based in Secunda, Mpumalanga, in South Africa. I help teams get coding agents to write
      code that fits their codebase, not just code that compiles.
    </p>
    <p>
      I built my first websites in WordPress during a high-school holiday job. I went on to study IT at North-West
      University in Potchefstroom (BSc IT, 2021 to 2024), doing freelance graphic and web design alongside my studies.
    </p>
    <p>
      Since 2025 I’ve worked as a full-stack developer: first on React and Next.js front-ends, and now remotely on
      enterprise .NET and Angular software.
    </p>
    <p>
      Outside work I build games with coding agents: a satirical power-grid sim about load shedding, a few
      prototypes, and one very silly weekend project. Long projects with lots of moving parts are a good test of
      orchestration.
    </p>
    <p>
      I speak English and Afrikaans, and some Dutch. I’m interested in the ethics of AI, and I’ve written about
      <a href={article}>why I’d rather call it a lazy optimizer than intelligent</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The best way to reach me is <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>, or see
      <a href="/work-with-me/">how we could work together</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
